MID_EV14_030_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_030_m01_001: I'm here, Kalla. And I'm so sorry I kept you waiting.
MID_EV14_030_m01_002: Ah, Leilidahna. I must say, your last match\nwas spectacular.
MID_EV14_030_m01_003: Watching you fight...I felt something light up\nwithin me.
MID_EV14_030_m01_004: Hmm, that's strange. I've only ever heard you say\nyou don't like to watch the fights.
MID_EV14_030_m01_005: I do not. However, when I saw how the battle\nignited your soul, Leilidahna...it pierced my heart.
MID_EV14_030_m01_006: In that moment, I realized how foolish I had been to\nask you to end your quest for revenge.
MID_EV14_030_m01_007: I wanted you to forgo vengeance and instead find a\nlife filled with peace.
MID_EV14_030_m01_008: But watching you in battle, I could see that one thing\nonly keeps your soul shining brightly...
MID_EV14_030_m01_009: And that is the powerful feelings you have\nfor Bertrand.
MID_EV14_030_m01_010: I also realized that taking that away from you would\nnot make you happy.
MID_EV14_030_m01_011: Leilidahna, I will no longer try to stop you. Let your\nsoul burn as brightly and as fiercely as you desire.
MID_EV14_030_m01_012: <NCA>Thank her.
MID_EV14_030_m01_013: Thank you, Kalla.
MID_EV14_030_m01_014: That said, the Heroic Games attract thousands of the\nstrongest combatants from every corner of the land.
MID_EV14_030_m01_015: There may yet be some extremely powerful and\nskilled fighters in the mix. Be on your guard.
MID_EV14_030_m01_016: That reminds me—I heard that Miss Leda might\nhave a visitor?
MID_EV14_030_m01_017: Oh yes, we've received word about your next match.\nYou may enter, Anna.
MID_EV14_030_m01_018: Listen up! Incoming Anna administrative\nannouncement for the Heroic Games!
MID_EV14_030_m01_019: Congratulations to Rose Tempest for winning the\nfirst round in the qualifiers!
MID_EV14_030_m01_020: That fight of yours was fantastic. The Heroic Games\nare a lot more exciting now that you've joined.
MID_EV14_030_m01_021: Ah, so you're the visitor.
MID_EV14_030_m01_022: Since you came all this way, perhaps you might join\nme after this? I can be very entertaining.
MID_EV14_030_m01_023: Sorry to disappoint you. Not only am I a busy\nwoman but I've heard rumors about you, Syracusio.
MID_EV14_030_m01_024: You know, if your womanizing gets too out of hand,\nyou might get a scolding from the Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV14_030_m01_025: Well, we can't have that. I politely withdraw\nmy invitation.
MID_EV14_030_m01_026: Can we please get back to the point?
MID_EV14_030_m01_027: Great idea. The date for your next match has\nbeen set.
MID_EV14_030_m01_028: I have all of the details here, so please take\na good look.
MID_EV14_030_m01_029: <TLP>Rose Tempest\n\nMatch: Second Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Silver Knights of Tellus\nLeader: Alexandra\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV14_030_m01_030: Are we gonna have allies from other clans like\nlast time?
MID_EV14_030_m01_031: Yup! That's how the qualifying rounds are arranged.
MID_EV14_030_m01_032: Though you'll have to wait until the day of the match\nto find out who you'll be working with.
MID_EV14_030_m01_033: And I'm sorry about this, but there isn't a lot of time\nbefore you're up.
MID_EV14_030_m01_034: That's no excuse for a poor performance. Just\nprepare as much as you can between now and then!
MID_EV14_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_031_m01_001: Is that Miss Leda? Something's not right...
MID_EV14_031_m01_002: *sigh*
MID_EV14_031_m01_003: What is happening? Is that a...a monster appearing\nbefore her?!
MID_EV14_031_m01_004: Kyagh!
MID_EV14_031_m01_005: Miss Leda! Get back!
MID_EV14_031_m01_006: Someone! Anyone! We need help!
MID_EV14_031_m01_007: What is going on?! Wh-what the hell is that?!
MID_EV14_031_m01_008: Aah... That's the...the...
MID_EV14_031_m01_009: Calm down. It's alright. It disappears when I do this.
MID_EV14_031_m01_010: Gyaah! Urgggh...
MID_EV14_031_m01_011: You WILL explain yourself, Leilidahna! What\nexactly happened back there?
MID_EV14_031_m01_012: *sigh* Fine. You've seen it, so I may as well explain.
MID_EV14_031_m01_013: Many songs about the Virtuosa of Heaven and Earth\nhave been passed among the bards.
MID_EV14_031_m01_014: One of those songs tells the story of how she used\nher vihuela to summon and control Demonic Beasts.
MID_EV14_031_m01_015: Obsidian used to belong to this Virtuosa of Heaven\nand Earth...
MID_EV14_031_m01_016: So, I thought I might be able to use it for summoning\nand controlling beasts too. I've been experimenting...
MID_EV14_031_m01_017: But it's not going very well. So far, the only things\nI've conjured are these deformed creatures.
MID_EV14_031_m01_018: Is one of these Demonic Beasts of yours the Phantom\nthat's been frightening people lately?
MID_EV14_031_m01_019: Yeah, that was one of mine. Defective. Same as what\nyou just saw.
MID_EV14_031_m01_020: I've practiced so many times...but they're still nothing\nlike the Demonic Beasts the virtuosa summoned.
MID_EV14_031_m01_021: One of them ran away before I could get rid of it.\nSo it's still lurking around the city somewhere.
MID_EV14_031_m01_022: Wait. So, this Phantom thing that's been terrifying\neveryone...is your fault?
MID_EV14_031_m01_023: Seriously?!
MID_EV14_031_m01_024: Listen, I...I know I'm in the wrong here.
MID_EV14_031_m01_025: I've been trying to find it at night so I can get\nrid of it.
MID_EV14_031_m01_026: Ah, so that's why you've been sneaking out.
MID_EV14_031_m01_027: But why would you try something so dangerous in\nthe first place?
MID_EV14_031_m01_028: What happened with Lechner before... It made me\npainfully aware of how lacking my skills are.
MID_EV14_031_m01_029: And I'm afraid our enemies will turn out to be so\nmuch more powerful than we thought.
MID_EV14_031_m01_030: Even so, milady, please stop putting yourself in\nharm's way like this.
MID_EV14_031_m01_031: Look, if I can't learn to control these Demonic Beasts,\nthen I have no hope of getting my revenge.
MID_EV14_031_m01_032: I need a new and more powerful ability. There's\nno other way.
MID_EV14_103_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_103_m01_001: Hmm...
MID_EV14_103_m01_002: What's wrong? You're not acting like, well...you.
MID_EV14_103_m01_003: I was looking at our next opponent—Alexandra—and\nwas suddenly reminded of home.
MID_EV14_103_m01_004: Oh, but I wish you hadn't seen me like this.
MID_EV14_103_m01_005: Never mind. I suppose it's fine. I've been desperate\nto talk to someone anyway.
MID_EV14_103_m01_006: You see, there's something that's been on my mind\nfor a very long time.
MID_EV14_103_m01_007: It's just... I have this idea that a person's life is almost\nlike the life of a flower.
MID_EV14_103_m01_008: Flowers sprout, grow tall, and form buds. Their\nbuds bloom...they bear fruit...then wither away.
MID_EV14_103_m01_009: Seeds fall from that fruit, and another new sprout\nemerges. And such is the life of a flower. That is all.
MID_EV14_103_m01_010: But I've always asked myself, "Is that really the life\nI want?"
MID_EV14_103_m01_011: I've never been comfortable with the idea of\nbearing children and growing a family.
MID_EV14_103_m01_012: Instead, I've wanted to wear beautiful clothes and to\ncatch the attention of all sorts of beautiful people.
MID_EV14_103_m01_013: I've wanted to feel my heart flutter as handsome men\ncourted me and to live out a storybook love affair.
MID_EV14_103_m01_014: More than anything, I've wanted to shine so very\nbrightly as I live my life.
MID_EV14_103_m01_015: I sound foolish when I say these things, don't I?\nYou must think I am vanity itself.
MID_EV14_103_m01_016: Not really. I think it makes sense for you. And there's\nnothing wrong with living the life you want to live.
MID_EV14_103_m01_017: Really? I'm surprised to hear you say that.
MID_EV14_103_m01_018: Yes, I believe that all people should live and\nblossom in their own way.
MID_EV14_103_m01_019: And thinking about it like that somehow makes\nme feel better.
MID_EV14_103_m01_020: I choose to blossom into the most spectacular flower.\nAnd when that flower withers away...
MID_EV14_103_m01_021: it will have left such a striking impression on all who\nlaid eyes upon it that it will never, ever be forgotten.
MID_EV14_103_m01_022: Most importantly, it will be a flower that pleases me\nmore than anyone else.
MID_EV14_103_m01_023: But I do sometimes worry that thinking like this\nmakes me horribly egotistical.
MID_EV14_103_m01_024: I feel guilty...like I should apologize to my father\nand to my house.
MID_EV14_103_m01_025: Really? Parents will have expectations, but in the\nend each child must decide how to live for themself.
MID_EV14_103_m01_026: And besides, I like the way you've thought about\nthis, Olympia.
MID_EV14_103_m01_027: I...was not expecting you to be so supportive. I'm\nhonestly not sure what to say.
MID_EV14_103_m01_028: Please. Just say, "Thank you, Leilidahna!" I'm sure a\nflower as spectacular as you can say what she means.
MID_EV14_033_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_033_m01_001: *sigh*
MID_EV14_033_m01_002: What is it, Miss Leda? You've had something on your\nmind since the match.
MID_EV14_033_m01_003: You saw it, didn't you—the incredible power that\nTheodora wielded?
MID_EV14_033_m01_004: I wonder if the queen's right arm...is also one\nof Drake's treasures.
MID_EV14_033_m01_005: I had the same thought, and I think it must be.
MID_EV14_033_m01_006: At the time, I sensed an incredible power coming\nfrom the queen.
MID_EV14_033_m01_007: I knew at once that I'd never be able to match her.\nBut then I had a thought...
MID_EV14_033_m01_008: Maybe I've only unleashed a small fraction of\nObsidian's power.
MID_EV14_033_m01_009: Miss Leda, please. You can't—
MID_EV14_033_m01_010: If I could awaken the power still hidden within\nObsidian...
MID_EV14_033_m01_011: If I could just go deeper, to a more\ntreacherous place...
MID_EV14_033_m01_012: Perhaps I could draw even more power\nfrom Obsidian.
MID_EV14_033_m01_013: That's too dangerous. You know what happens to\nthose who become enslaved by Drake's treasures.
MID_EV14_033_m01_014: You would only bring about your own ruin faster...
MID_EV14_033_m01_015: Think about the state Queen Theodora was in.
MID_EV14_033_m01_016: She almost didn't return to her senses.
MID_EV14_033_m01_017: Sirocco, I wonder if you've ever heard this rumor...
MID_EV14_033_m01_018: Those who travel to the underworld and make it out\nalive receive a power—a blessing—from Balor.
MID_EV14_033_m01_019: If that's true, the closer to death I get, the stronger\nthe power I'll receive...
MID_EV14_033_m01_020: Stop! This is a foolish line of thought, and Kalla\nwould never want this for you.
MID_EV14_033_m01_021: Please. I won't die. Do you really think I'd let myself\ndie before killing Bertrand?
MID_EV14_033_m01_022: Besides, if we don't have enough power to beat our\nenemies, then what's the point?
MID_EV14_033_m01_023: It's simple. If I want more power, I have to give more\nof myself than I ever have before.